{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/890","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Finding Words","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","id":"actor/1","type":"Actor"},{"_label":null,"id":"actor/401","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"O’Keeffe repeatedly remarked that words did not suffice when it came to expressing herself. Nonetheless, she often wrote in support of her work and was a prolific correspondent writing daily for personal and professional purposes. Writing to family, friends, and an interesting circle of colleagues, O’Keeffe’s letters document and offer a glimpse into the passions, triumphs, and dialing happenings of O’Keeffe’s life.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}